{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3096","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3096","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3096\",\"parent_revision\":\"69210b46999bea0e7d50288fbdffdd27ccc853b0945880c039d6fd58518e4d7a\",\"root_revision\":\"69210b46999bea0e7d50288fbdffdd27ccc853b0945880c039d6fd58518e4d7a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-20\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe `complete-implementation` skill (`plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md`) has no step that opens a PR and no step that monitors a PR for reviews after work lands. Confirmed by direct read: SKILL.md's \\\"Final Step: Commit and Push Remaining Changes\\\" section commits and pushes to a branch, then proceeds straight to \\\"Final Handoff Output\\\" (`references/final-handoff.md`) \u2014 neither file contains any `gh pr create`, \\\"pull request\\\", or review-related step.\\n\\nThe workflow must be updated so that, as part of completing an implementation:\\n\\n1. A PR is opened for the work if one does not already exist.\\n2. After opening (or once an existing PR is confirmed), the agent must monitor that PR for CI status, review comments, and inline code suggestions \u2014 polling until CI completes and reviews have had a chance to land, not declaring done immediately after push.\\n3. Each review finding (bot or human) must be assessed against the actual current source and the task's original goal/acceptance criteria before acting on it \u2014 never blindly accepted or blindly dismissed.\\n4. Confirmed findings must be fixed, and dismissed findings must have their rebuttal reasoning stated.\\n5. After any fix, the same PR must be re-checked (CI re-run, no new unaddressed findings) before the loop is considered closed.\\n6. This monitor-assess-act-verify cycle repeats until the PR is clean, not a single pass.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: \\\"This is the same discipline already used manually, repeatedly, in this session's PR work (dispatching a fork to poll gh pr checks and gh api .../comments with --paginate, verifying each bot finding against real source before fixing or rebutting it, re-verifying after every fix round, only merging once clean) \u2014 it needs to be a codified step in complete-implementation's own pipeline, not something the orchestrating agent has to remember to do manually each time.\\\"\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **feat: complete-implementation must open and monitor a pr through review to closure** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task - auto-derived from input\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-20\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Scope Update 2026 08 24\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe `receiving-pr-reviews` skill landed on `main` at `8efe217d8`\\n(`.agents/skills/receiving-pr-reviews/SKILL.md`, symlinked from `.claude/skills/`), and\\n`AGENTS.md`'s inline PR Review Protocol was replaced by a two-line pointer to it. That skill\\nimplements most of what this issue asked for. Remaining scope is narrower than the original\\ndescription.\\n\\nNow covered by `receiving-pr-reviews` \u2014 items 2 through 6 of the description:\\n\\n- Fetch every unresolved thread and every review carrying a top-level body, auto-paginated, via\\n  `scripts/pr_review_threads.py fetch`. The skill also documents the trap this issue's manual\\n  practice hit: an empty `unresolved` array is not \\\"nothing to do\\\" \u2014 `reviews_count`,\\n  `threads_count`, and `unresolved_count` must be read together, and a top-level `COMMENTED` or\\n  approving review with no inline comment surfaces only through `reviews_with_body`.\\n- Validate each finding locally against actual current source before acting (step 2).\\n- Fix, commit, and push before replying, so the SHA named in the reply is inspectable (step 3).\\n- Reply on the thread with the disposition \u2014 conclusion, evidence, SHA, or the rebuttal reasoning\\n  when no change was warranted (step 4) \u2014 then resolve it (step 5).\\n- Re-check for new activity on a bounded schedule via the `watch` subcommand, looped as short calls\\n  (step 7), which is the monitor-assess-act-verify cycle repeating until clean rather than a single\\n  pass.\\n\\nStill outstanding \u2014 the part this issue should now track:\\n\\n1. Opening the PR. `complete-implementation/SKILL.md` still has no `gh pr create` step; its Final\\n   Step commits and pushes to a branch and proceeds to the final handoff.\\n2. Pipeline integration. Verified 2026-08-24: `receiving-pr-reviews` is referenced from\\n   `AGENTS.md:474` and nowhere else \u2014 no plugin skill, agent, or rule points at it, so\\n   `/dh:complete-implementation` does not reach it on its own. Note the boundary: this skill is\\n   repo-root content in `.agents/skills/`, while `complete-implementation` is\\n   development-harness plugin content shipped to consumers, so the integration cannot be a\\n   relative path into this checkout.\\n3. Passing the originating issue reference into the loop, so findings can be assessed against the\\n   issue's acceptance criteria and not only against the diff.\\n\\nOut of scope here, tracked separately: whether a review round verifies the PR demonstrates it\\nresolves the issue is #3220. That check's assessment unit is the issue's acceptance criteria\\nagainst the merged diff; this issue's loop assesses review findings. The two compose \u2014 the loop is\\nwhere that check would run, and #3220 is the check the loop currently lacks. The commit and PR-body\\nreference convention that makes deferred closure work is #3219.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"26d775a634fad6947a58b1a5439a275d9fa0ab45fa89d6a0cbf124f6cb1004ef\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQVp0Xw\"}"}